WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.101
Open Ava's Playground, then choose Edit world.

2
00:00:03.101 --> 00:00:08.211
The editor sits below the journey, so you can change the challenge and

3
00:00:08.211 --> 00:00:09.783
return to watching Ava.

4
00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:14.500
This example uses the supplied trained model and its small saved room.

5
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.173
Choose Toggle walls, then click an empty square to add a wall.

6
00:00:20.173 --> 00:00:22.782
Click that wall again to remove it.

7
00:00:22.782 --> 00:00:27.627
You are changing the problem Ava faces, not writing the moves that solve

8
00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.000
it.

9
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.106
Choose Lamp, then click a clear square to move the destination.

10
00:00:33.106 --> 00:00:35.592
The Ava tool moves her starting place.

11
00:00:35.592 --> 00:00:40.209
The route message checks whether a journey is possible under the world rules.

12
00:00:40.209 --> 00:00:43.050
It doesn't prove the model can find it.

13
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.099
Compatible layout edits keep the learned weights.

14
00:00:47.099 --> 00:00:52.390
Try the changed world before retraining, so you can see what the model

15
00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:53.203
already handles.

16
00:00:53.203 --> 00:00:56.866
Larger sixteen-by-sixteen worlds also support coloured keys and doors.

17
00:00:56.866 --> 00:01:01.750
Expanding an old small room changes its input format and requires retraining.

18
00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:07.517
If you want Ava to learn navigation for a challenge, open Training and

19
00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:08.571
choose useful practice.

20
00:01:08.571 --> 00:01:13.137
Read the reset message before changing her practice choices: those changes start her

21
00:01:13.137 --> 00:01:13.840
learning afresh.

22
00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.650
Training and editing the room are separate actions.
